A||N||3||Verticalspeed||Freaky Wiring???||||1||
Z||000000||Verticalspeed||12-24-2000||11:53 PM||||I have a Valentine ONE radar detector. Basic power and ground installation. However, when I depress the brakes, the radar reactivates itself, like it loses current when the brakes are applied. Why is this happening? I checked the ground for the unit, and it's the way it's supposed to be. Good ground.<BR>What gives?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/police4.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||12-25-2000||04:12 AM||||I would check the grounds on the engine and frame, and the alternator.  If the detector is really sensitive the sudden current drop from the brake lights turning on could cause it to reset...  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||12-25-2000||11:58 AM||||Possibly also try a different power source, i.e. a different circut.  If you've already got it on its own circut, then it must be the ground.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-25-2000||04:41 PM||||whered you tie the hot in, i used a lead straight to fusebox, but I hear they recommend tying it to dome lite hot wire. I like mine to turn off and on with ign key.||||reg||1
